1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:02,230
When you tell Noah your PC is slow,

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,960
it doesn't immediately start changing things.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,030
First, Noah checks what's actually happening.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,230
Then it explains what it found…

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,360
…and shows you what it recommends.

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,800
Before anything changes, Noah asks for your approval.

7
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,850
You decide what happens next.

8
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,380
If you approve it, Noah performs the supported actions…

9
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,480
…and then shows you what changed.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,630
That's the idea behind Noah: describe it, approve it, done.

11
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:44,710
Free PC Check at onnoah.app
